From f048b97c9506123f81206b38108570eb99dce4cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 18:32:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make the search answer exactly, stop copying the repetition
 map, and add contempt

- The transposition cache stored a node's value after an alpha-beta cutoff
  as if it were exact; at depth 4 that changed the chosen move in 2 of 60
  sampled positions. It now stores exact/lower/upper flags and a bound
  narrows the window. Over the same 60 positions the cached search equals
  the uncached one equals the old uncached one. 1.48x faster than the
  shipped engine over twelve depth-4 positions.
- The search shares the root's repetition map read-only and counts
  repetition along its own path (applyLegalAction(..., false)); the search
  no longer slows as a game lengthens (1.9x -> 1.00x at 150 entries).
- A draw is worth CONTEMPT (60) against the side choosing. Sharp-vs-Sharp
  repetition draws: 14 of 16 -> 11 of 16; at 300 they become 100-move
  games, so the rest is the game's. Sharp's moves change on purpose.
- DECISIONS.md: the occupant patch's 1.2x did not reproduce on a quiet
  CPU and is withdrawn; the record says so.

CACHE v43 -> v44.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
