+
+**The bot has contempt.** A draw is worth `CONTEMPT` (60, a fifth of a knight) against the side
+choosing, so it repeats a position only when it is worse off than that. Sixteen Sharp-vs-Sharp games
+from every king placement: 14 repetition draws before, 11 after, and with contempt raised to 300 the
+draws become six 100-move games with no result. So the drawishness is mostly the game's, not the
+search's: on a 4×4 board where a drop may not give check, the side with nothing better to do can
+usually hold. Steady (depth 3) is unaffected: 6–6 with four games past 100 moves. **This changes
